<div class="mb-8">
  <Heading size="2xl" as="h1" class="mb-2">Typography</Heading>
  <Text size="lg" tone="subdued" as="h2">
    Semantic typography components that map to the correct HTML elements with consistent,
    opinionated styling for each variant.
  </Text>
</div>

<!-- Canonical example -->
<div class="mb-8">
  <Example source={'
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <Typography variant="h2">The Joke Tax Chronicles</Typography>
      <Typography variant="p">Once upon a time, in a far-off land, there was a very lazy king.</Typography>
    </div>
  '}/>
</div>

<!-- Usage -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Usage</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-card overflow-hidden">
    <CodeBlock code={"<Typography variant=\"h1\">Page Title</Typography>\n<Typography variant=\"lead\">A lead paragraph.</Typography>\n<Typography variant=\"muted\">Muted footnote text.</Typography>"}/>
  </div>
  <Prose class="mt-4">
    <p>
      Typography renders a single element with a predefined style based on its <code>variant</code>.
      Each variant maps to a specific HTML tag and CSS treatment — <code>h1</code> renders an
      <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>, <code>lead</code> renders a <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> with larger
      muted text, <code>blockquote</code> renders a <code>&lt;blockquote&gt;</code> with a left
      border, and so on.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- When to Use -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">When to Use</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Use Typography when you want a quick, opinionated text element with both the right HTML
      tag and visual style chosen for you. It's ideal for content pages, marketing layouts, and
      anywhere you want consistent typographic hierarchy without composing
      <a href="/components/heading">Heading</a> and <a href="/components/text">Text</a> manually.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you need fine-grained control over size, weight, and tone independently, use
      <a href="/components/heading">Heading</a> and <a href="/components/text">Text</a> directly.
      For long-form content with mixed HTML elements (paragraphs, lists, links, code), use
      <a href="/components/prose">Prose</a> which styles children automatically.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Behaviour -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Behaviour</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      The <code>variant</code> prop determines both the HTML tag and the visual style. The
      mapping is fixed:
    </p>
  </Prose>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden mt-4">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Variant</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">HTML Tag</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y">
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">h1</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">&lt;h1&gt;</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Page title — largest heading</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">h2</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">&lt;h2&gt;</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Section heading</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">h3</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">&lt;h3&gt;</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Subsection heading</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">h4</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">&lt;h4&gt;</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Minor heading</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">p</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">&lt;p&gt;</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Standard paragraph</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">blockquote</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">&lt;blockquote&gt;</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Callout or citation with left border</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">list</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">&lt;ul&gt;</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Unordered list</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">lead</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">&lt;p&gt;</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Introductory paragraph — larger, muted</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">large</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">&lt;div&gt;</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Large emphasized text</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">small</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">&lt;small&gt;</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Fine print</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">muted</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">&lt;p&gt;</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Secondary text — smaller, muted color</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Examples -->
<div class="flex flex-col gap-12 mb-12">
  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">All Variants</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Every available typography variant with its rendered output.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <Typography variant="h1">Heading 1</Typography>
        <Typography variant="h2">Heading 2</Typography>
        <Typography variant="h3">Heading 3</Typography>
        <Typography variant="h4">Heading 4</Typography>
        <Typography variant="p">A paragraph of body text with default styling.</Typography>
        <Typography variant="blockquote">A blockquote for callouts or citations.</Typography>
        <Typography variant="lead">Lead text for introductory paragraphs.</Typography>
        <Typography variant="large">Large text for emphasis.</Typography>
        <Typography variant="small">Small text for fine print.</Typography>
        <Typography variant="muted">Muted text for secondary information.</Typography>
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Article Layout</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Compose variants to build a content page with proper typographic hierarchy.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 max-w-lg">
        <Typography variant="h1">Getting Started</Typography>
        <Typography variant="lead">Everything you need to know to start building with Orbital.</Typography>
        <Typography variant="h2">Installation</Typography>
        <Typography variant="p">Add the gem to your Gemfile and run bundle install. The library ships with all components, styles, and JavaScript controllers.</Typography>
        <Typography variant="blockquote">Orbital requires Ruby 3.2+ and Rails 7.1+.</Typography>
        <Typography variant="muted">Last updated July 2026.</Typography>
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Best Practices -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Best Practices</Heading>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-green-500/30 bg-green-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-green-600">Do</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Use Typography for content pages where you want quick, consistent hierarchy.</li>
          <li>Follow heading order (<code>h1</code> &rarr; <code>h2</code> &rarr; <code>h3</code>) for accessibility.</li>
          <li>Use <code>lead</code> for the introductory paragraph of a page or section.</li>
          <li>Use <code>muted</code> for timestamps, footnotes, and secondary metadata.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-red-600">Don't</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Mix Typography with Heading/Text for the same content — pick one approach per page.</li>
          <li>Skip heading levels (<code>h1</code> &rarr; <code>h3</code>) — it breaks document outline.</li>
          <li>Use heading variants just for visual size — choose the variant for its semantic meaning.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- API Reference -->
<div>
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">API Reference</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Prop</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Type</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Values</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Default</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y">
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">variant</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Symbol</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">h1, h2, h3, h4, p, blockquote, list, lead, large, small, muted</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">p</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
